Float conversion latency of the game's retail compiler (notes/COMPILER.md, "Float
conversion latency"), for the build psp-gcc-4.0.4a: the LBP-PSP-Decomp kit's
psp-gcc-4.0.4c work tree plus this diff and block-move-4.0.4.diff
(tools/gcc/build_404a.sh). Applies with `patch -p1` in gcc-4.0.4/ after the kit's diffs.
In config/mips/allegrex-sched.md, the kit's Allegrex scheduling description: an `fcvt`
instruction (trunc.w.s, cvt.s.w...) gets a latency of 2 instead of generic.md's 1, so
the scheduler puts an independent instruction between it and the mfc1 that reads it.
2 and 3 give the same code on every Bullet file; 2 is the smallest that matches.
The kit's context is GPL-3.0-or-later.
--- a/gcc/config/mips/allegrex-sched.md
+++ b/gcc/config/mips/allegrex-sched.md
@@ -7,3 +7,7 @@
 (define_insn_reservation "alg_store" 1
   (and (eq_attr "cpu" "allegrex") (eq_attr "type" "store,fpstore,fpidxstore"))
   "alu+alg_mem,alg_mem*2")
+;; game: float conversions (trunc.w.s, cvt.s.w...) take 2 cycles or more
+(define_insn_reservation "alg_fcvt" 2
+  (and (eq_attr "cpu" "allegrex") (eq_attr "type" "fcvt"))
+  "alu")
